@startuml agent-concept-layers
' ============================================================================
'  Concept map: Tool vs Connector vs Channel vs MCP vs Plugin vs Skill,
'  shown as containment layers ("circles within circles") for BOTH
'  the Claude ecosystem and OpenClaw.
'
'  Reading rule: the model in the centre can ONLY call TOOLS. Every box that
'  WRAPS a tool is just packaging that delivers tools (+ instructions) to it.
'
'  Render: java -jar ../../../plantuml.jar -tpng agent-concept-layers.puml
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam nodesep 14
skinparam ranksep 26
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #777777
  FontStyle bold
  FontSize 14
}
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #888888
  roundCorner 14
  FontStyle bold
}

title Layers of capability - what contains what\n(orange = TOOL | blue = one-service integration | purple = bundle | green = instructions)

' ----- the universal centre -------------------------------------------------
rectangle "AGENT LOOP / LLM\n**can ONLY call Tools**" as CORE #FFFFFF

' ===========================================================================
'  CLAUDE
' ===========================================================================
package "CLAUDE  (claude.ai / Desktop / Code)" #FFF3E0 {

  rectangle "**PLUGIN** - distributable bundle\n(installed from a marketplace)" as C_PLUGIN #E1BEE7 {

    rectangle "Slash commands" as C_CMD #ECEFF1
    rectangle "Subagents" as C_AGT #ECEFF1
    rectangle "Hooks" as C_HOOK #ECEFF1
    rectangle "**Skill**\nSKILL.md = on-demand instructions" as C_SKILL #C8E6C9

    rectangle "**CONNECTOR** = remote MCP server\n(one SaaS, OAuth: Gmail / Notion / Figma)" as C_CONN #BBDEFB {
      rectangle "Tool\n(read_email)" as C_T1 #FFE0B2
      rectangle "Tool\n(send_email)" as C_T2 #FFE0B2
    }
  }
}

' ===========================================================================
'  OPENCLAW
' ===========================================================================
package "OPENCLAW" #E8F0FE {

  rectangle "**PLUGIN / EXTENSION** - ownership bundle\n(owns a whole company or feature)" as O_PLUGIN #E1BEE7 {

    rectangle "Capabilities\n(provider / speech / web-search contracts)" as O_CAP #ECEFF1
    rectangle "CLI commands / HTTP routes / services" as O_CLI #ECEFF1
    rectangle "Hooks" as O_HOOK #ECEFF1
    rectangle "**Skill**\ncontent pack (instructions)" as O_SKILL #C8E6C9

    rectangle "**CHANNEL** = messaging surface\n(Slack / Discord / WhatsApp)" as O_CHAN #BBDEFB {
      rectangle "shared **message** Tool" as O_T1 #FFE0B2
    }

    rectangle "**MCP server** = external tools" as O_MCP #BBDEFB {
      rectangle "Tool" as O_T2 #FFE0B2
    }
  }
}

' ----- the model only ever touches the orange (tool) layer -------------------
CORE --> C_T1 : calls
CORE --> C_T2 : calls
CORE --> O_T1 : calls
CORE --> O_T2 : calls
CORE ..> C_SKILL : reads instructions
CORE ..> O_SKILL : reads instructions

note bottom of CORE
  **Same rule on both sides:**
  1. TOOL (orange) = the atom the model actually invokes.
  2. CONNECTOR / CHANNEL / MCP (blue) = ONE service's set of tools.
  3. PLUGIN (purple) = a bundle that may hold many of the blue boxes
     PLUS commands, agents, hooks and skills.
  4. SKILL (green) = instructions injected into context, not a callable.

  "Connector" is a Claude word; OpenClaw splits the same idea into
  **Channel** (chat surfaces) + **MCP server** (external tools).
  Blue boxes can also exist standalone - they don't *need* a plugin.
end note

@enduml
